# HTTP response headers for static hosting (Netlify / Cloudflare Pages /
# Vercel-equivalent). Astro copies files in `public/` to `dist/` at build
# time, so this file lands at the site root and is picked up
# automatically by the host's `_headers` convention.
#
# THIS FILE IS ENFORCED BY THE BUILD. `prehighlight.mjs` (the last step of
# `npm run build`) parses the CSP below, walks every built HTML file, and
# fails the build if the page contains an inline <script> whose hash is not
# listed here, or an inline <style> element at all. So an Astro/Starlight
# upgrade that changes a boot script breaks the *build*, not the deployed
# site. When it does, the failure prints the corrected `script-src` to paste.
#
# CSP audit, 2026-09-07, measured against the 69 built HTML pages and every
# JS/CSS asset in `dist/` (not assumed):
#
# - `script-src` lists nine sha256 hashes instead of `'unsafe-inline'`. All
#   nine are Starlight's own boot scripts (theme provider + picker, search
#   shortcut key, language select, sidebar state persistence + scroll
#   restore, mobile menu button). None is ours: the tour client loads as
#   `<script type="module" src="/nomi/tour-client.mjs">`, so it is covered by
#   `'self'`. The bodies carry no per-page or content-hashed text, so the
#   nine hashes cover all 69 pages.
# - `script-src 'wasm-unsafe-eval'` is required by the Go interpreter wasm,
#   the tree-sitter wasm, and Pagefind's search wasm. `'unsafe-eval'` is NOT
#   required: the only `eval` in the vendored `web-tree-sitter.js` is
#   Emscripten's EM_ASM/EM_JS support, and our grammar wasm has no such
#   section.
# - `style-src-elem 'self'` — zero inline <style> elements in the build, and
#   nothing injects one at runtime. (Pagefind ships a
#   `pagefind-highlight.js` that would, but nothing in the build references
#   it.) Browsers without `style-src-elem` (Firefox) fall back to
#   `style-src`, so the tightening is additive and never breaks a browser.
# - `style-src-attr 'unsafe-inline'` is forced by 8752 inline `style="..."`
#   attributes across the build, 19 distinct values: Starlight's sidebar
#   `--depth`, its `--sl-icon-size` / `--sl-select-width` custom properties,
#   and Shiki's per-token `color:` on the Go code blocks. Attribute hashes
#   would need `'unsafe-hashes'`, which is not supported everywhere and buys
#   nothing against 19 build-generated values.
# - `style-src 'self' 'unsafe-inline'` remains only as the fallback for
#   browsers that do not implement the `-elem`/`-attr` split.
# - `img-src data:` is forced by 18 `url("data:image/svg+xml...")`
#   backgrounds in the built CSS (Starlight's `common.css`, Pagefind's UI
#   CSS). CSS background images are fetched under `img-src`.
# - `worker-src 'self'` covers both workers, each constructed from a
#   same-origin URL: the tour's `/nomi/run-worker.js` and Pagefind's
#   `/pagefind/pagefind-worker.js`. No `blob:` needed.
# - `connect-src 'self'` blocks data exfiltration if the worker or wasm
#   ever fetches an attacker URL. The only legitimate fetches are
#   same-origin loads of /nomi/*.{wasm,js,scm,mjs} and Pagefind's index
#   fragments.
# - `base-uri 'none'`, `form-action 'none'`, `frame-src 'none'`: the build
#   contains zero <base>, <form>, <iframe>, <object> and <embed> elements
#   and no script creates one. (DOMPurify constructs a detached <form> for
#   its DOM-clobbering check and never submits it, so `form-action 'none'`
#   is safe.)
# - If a third-party service is added later (analytics, fonts on a CDN,
#   embed iframes), expand the relevant directive.
#
# What a visitor's program can reach, audited 2026-09-29 (roadmap "Tour
# public-deployment hardening"): nothing outside its worker. The stdlib has no
# networking module, and io.read_file/io.write_file are refused by the browser
# build itself (internal/stdio/file_browser.go, held by cmd/nomi-wasm's
# browser_build_test.go), so `connect-src 'self'` is a second wall rather
# than the only one. The wasm's memory is capped at 1 GiB
# (internal/wasmmem) and the page kills a run after 6 s.
#
# The other headers:
# - `frame-ancestors 'none'` plus `X-Frame-Options: DENY` for browsers that
#   predate CSP 2: the tour has no reason to be framed, and editable code
#   boxes are a clickjacking target.
# - `Cross-Origin-Resource-Policy: same-origin`: no other site may embed the
#   Nomi wasm (nomi.wasm.gz) or any other asset. Every fetch the site makes is
#   same-origin, so nothing here is affected.
# - `Cross-Origin-Opener-Policy: same-origin` severs window.opener from
#   cross-origin openers. COEP is deliberately NOT set: `require-corp` would
#   make the page cross-origin isolated, which unlocks SharedArrayBuffer and
#   high-resolution timers that nothing here uses and that only widen what a
#   page running visitors' code exposes.
# - `Permissions-Policy` turns off every powerful feature the site never uses.
#   Only feature names Chromium recognizes are listed, because an unknown one
#   is logged as a console error on every page.
#
# SRI is deliberately skipped — `marked` / `DOMPurify` / `web-tree-sitter`
# are all vendored same-origin (see `scripts/build-tour-wasm.sh`), so the
# same-origin guarantee + deployment integrity covers what SRI would.

